            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0746" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1068: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-15T20:00:00-03:30">May 15, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 15—8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. My 69, May 15, 11 a.m. Guani has just informed me that Cantilo accepts the
                    Uruguayan draft and withdraws his proposed modification to Buenos Aires and Rio
                    de Janeiro.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
